ned in section 2(b)),\n\n        (C) $250,000 in the case of an individual who is not married and who is not a surviving spouse or head of household, and\n\n        (D) 1/2 the amount applicable under subparagraph (A) in the case of a married individual filing a separate return."\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. **Filing Status**: Alice is married (married Dec 10, 2009) and files separately. Under §1(d), the tax rates for "Married individuals filing separate returns" apply.\n\n2. **Standard Deduction**: Alice takes the standard deduction. However, under §162(b)(6)(A), "a married individual filing a separate return where either spouse itemizes deductions" has a standard deduction of zero. Since Alice\'s husband itemizes deductions of $4,421, Alice\'s standard deduction = $0.\n\n3. **Exemptions**: Under §151(d)(1), the exemption amount is $2,000. Alice is entitled to her own exemption. However, under §151(b), the spouse exemption requires the spouse to have "no gross income". Alice\'s husband has gross income of $56,298, so Alice gets no spouse exemption. Alice has 1 exemption.\n\n4. **Exemption Phaseout**: Under §151(d)(3), the exemption is reduced by the applicable percentage if AGI exceeds the applicable amount. Under §68(b)(1)(D), the applicable amount for married filing separately is 1/2 of $300,000 = $150,000.\n\n   Computation for applicable percentage:\n   - AGI = $554,313\n   - Excess over $150,000 = $554,313 - $150,000 = $404,313\n   - For married filing separately, use $1,250 per §151(d)(3)(B)\n   - Number of $1,250 fractions = ceil($404,313 / $1,250) = ceil(323.4504) = 324\n   - Applicable percentage = 324 × 2% = 648%, capped at 100%\n   - Effective exemption = $2,000 × (1 - 1.0) = $0\n\n5. **Taxable Income**:\n   - Gross income: $554,313\n   - Less standard deduction: $0\n   - Less exemptions: $0 (100% phaseout)\n   - Taxable income = $554,313\n\n6. **Tax Calculation** under §1(d)(v):\n   - Taxable income $554,313 exceeds $125,000\n   - Tax = $37,764.25 + 39.6% × ($554,313 - $125,000)\n   - Tax = $37,764.25 + 0.396 × $429,313\n   - Tax = $37,764.25 + $170,007.948\n   - Tax = $207,772.198\n   - Rounded to whole number: $207,772\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 207772\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
