Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt << \'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\nSection 3306(a)(2)(B) (lines 265-272):\n\n"(2) Agricultural labor\n\nIn the case of agricultural labor, the term "employer" means, with respect to any calendar year, any person who-\n\n    (A) during the calendar year or the preceding calendar year paid wages of $20,000 or more for agricultural labor, or\n\n    (B) on each of some 10 days during the calendar year or during the preceding calendar year, each day being in a different calendar week, employed at least 5 individuals in employment in agricultural labor for some portion of the day."\n\n## Reasoning\n\nSection 3306(a)(2)(B) defines an employer for agricultural labor as a person who, on each of some 10 days during the calendar year (each day in a different calendar week), employed at least 5 individuals in agricultural labor.\n\nThe case facts show Alice employed agricultural workers on the following dates in 2017:\n- Jan 24: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred)\n- Feb 4: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred)\n- Mar 3: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred)\n- Mar 18: 5 employees (Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George)\n- Apr 1: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Fred, George)\n- May 9: 5 employees (Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George)\n- Oct 14: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, George)\n- Oct 25: 6 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George)\n- Nov 8: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Emily, Fred, George)\n- Nov 22: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred)\n- Dec 1: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, George)\n- Dec 2: 5 employees (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, George)\n\nUsing ISO calendar week calculation (as verified with Python):\n- Jan 24, 2017: Week 4\n- Feb 4, 2017: Week 5\n- Mar 3, 2017: Week 9\n- Mar 18, 2017: Week 11\n- Apr 1, 2017: Week 13\n- May 9, 2017: Week 19\n- Oct 14, 2017: Week 41\n- Oct 25, 2017: Week 43\n- Nov 8, 2017: Week 45\n- Nov 22, 2017: Week 47\n- Dec 1, 2017: Week 48\n- Dec 2, 2017: Week 48\n\nNumber of unique calendar weeks = 11 (computed: 12 dates - 1 duplicate week 48 = 11 unique weeks)\n\nSince 11 >= 10 (the threshold in Section 3306(a)(2)(B)), and each employment day had at least 5 employees (ranging from 5 to 6), Alice satisfies the condition in Section 3306(a)(2)(B) for 2017.\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: Entailment\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
