Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<\'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\n§2(b)(1) Definition of head of household (lines 212-230):\n"An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\n    (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\n        (ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151,\nFor purposes of this paragraph, an individual shall be considered as maintaining a household only if over half of the cost of maintaining the household during the taxable year is furnished by such individual."\n\n§152(d)(1) Qualifying relative (lines 148-150):\n"The term \'qualifying relative\' means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\n    (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\n    (B) who has no income for the calendar year in which such taxable year begins,\n    (D) who is not a qualifying child of such taxpayer or of any other taxpayer for any taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which such taxable year begins."\n\n§152(d)(2)(C) Relationship (line 165):\n"(C) The father or mother, or an ancestor of either."\n\n§151(b) Taxpayer and spouse (lines 50-55):\n"An exemption of the exemption amount for the taxpayer; and an additional exemption of the exemption amount for the spouse of the taxpayer if a joint return is not made by the taxpayer and his spouse..."\n\n§151(c) Additional exemption for dependents (lines 57-59):\n"An exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year."\n\n§151(d)(1) Exemption amount (lines 65-68):\n"Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \'exemption amount\' means $2,000."\n\n§151(d)(3)(A) Phaseout (lines 79-82):\n"In the case of any taxpayer whose adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b), the exemptionamount shall be reduced by the applicable percentage."\n\n§68(b)(1)(C) Applicable amount (lines 482-484):\n"(C) $250,000 in the case of an individual who is not married and who is not a surviving spouse or head of household, and"\n\n§1(b) Tax imposed - Heads of households (lines 23-30):\n"There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every head of a household (as defined in section 2(b)) a tax determined in accordance with the following:\n    (ii) $4,440, plus 28% of the excess over $29,600 if the taxable income is over $29,600 but not over $76,400;"\n\n§150(c)(2)(B) Basic standard deduction (lines 388-390):\n"(B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or"\n\n§150(b) Individuals who do not itemize their deductions (lines 362-370):\n"In the case of an individual who does not elect to itemize his deductions for the taxable year, for purposes of this subtitle, the term \'taxable income\' means adjusted gross income, minus-\n    (1) the standard deduction, and\n    (2) the deduction for personal exemptions provided in section 151."\n\n## Reasoning\n\n**Step 1: Determine Alice\'s filing status**\n\nAlice is unmarried (no spouse is mentioned in the facts). Under §2(b)(1), Alice qualifies as head of household because:\n- She is not married at the close of her taxable year\n- She maintains a household (the house she shares with Bob) as the principal place of abode for her father Bob for more than one-half of the taxable year (she has lived there since 2007)\n- She furnishes over half of the household costs (75%)\n- Bob is her dependent (see Step 2)\n\n**Step 2: Determine if Bob qualifies as a dependent**\n\nUnder §152(d)(1), Bob qualifies as a qualifying relative because:\n- §152(d)(2)(C): Bob is Alice\'s father (qualifying relationship)\n- The facts do not mention Bob having any income, so we assume he has no income as required by §152(d)(1)(B)\n- Bob is not a qualifying child (he is older than 25 years old)\n\n**Step 3: Calculate personal exemptions**\n\nUnder §151(b) and §151(c), Alice gets:\n- 1 exemption for herself = $2,000 (§151(d)(1))\n- 1 exemption for Bob (dependent) = $2,000 (§151(c))\n- Total exemptions = $4,000\n\n**Step 4: Check exemption phaseout**\n\nUnder §151(d)(3)(A), the exemption phaseout applies only if AGI exceeds the applicable amount under §68(b).\n\nUnder §68(b)(1)(C), the applicable amount for an unmarried individual is $250,000.\n\nAlice\'s AGI = $67,285 < $250,000, so no phaseout applies.\n\n**Step 5: Calculate taxable income**\n\nAlice itemizes deductions ($17,817 is given). Under §150(b), taxable income = AGI - itemized deductions - personal exemptions.\n\nTaxable income = $67,285 - $17,817 - $4,000 = $45,468\n\n**Step 6: Calculate tax**\n\nUnder §1(b)(ii) for head of households:\n- Taxable income of $45,468 is over $29,600 but not over $76,400\n- Tax = $4,440 + 28% of excess over $29,600\n- Excess = $45,468 - $29,600 = $15,868\n- Tax = $4,440 + 0.28 × $15,868 = $4,440 + $4,443.04 = $8,883.04\n\nRounded to the nearest whole dollar: $8,883\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 8883\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
