o be considered "employment", the employee must be "a citizen of the United States as an employee of an American employer."\n\n3. Section 3306(c)(1) (lines 315-327) provides an exception for agricultural labor, but this exception only applies to services that already qualify under Section 3306(c)(B) - meaning Bob must be a US citizen.\n\n4. The case facts do NOT specify that Bob is a citizen of the United States.\n\n5. Since Bob\'s citizenship is not established as a US citizen, Section 3306(c)(B) does not apply, and therefore Section 3306(c)(1) cannot apply either.\n\n6. The claim that "Section 3306(c)(1) applies to Alice employing Bob for the year 2017" is FALSE because the prerequisite condition (Bob being a US citizen) is not met.\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: Contradiction\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
