Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<\'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\n### §1(b) Tax imposed on heads of households\nLines 20-27:\n"There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every head of a household (as defined in section 2(b)) a tax determined in accordance with the following:\n    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $29,600;"\n\n### §2(a)(1) Definition of surviving spouse\nLines 186-195:\n"(1) In general\n    For purposes of section 1, the term \'surviving spouse\' means a taxpayer-\n        (A) whose spouse died during either of the two years immediately preceding the taxable year, and\n        (B) who maintains as his home a household which constitutes for the taxable year the principal place of abode (as a member of such household) of a dependent (i) who (within the meaning of section 152) is a son, stepson, daughter, or stepdaughter of the taxpayer, and (ii) with respect to whom the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year under section 151."\n\n### §2(b)(1) Definition of head of household\nLines 200-215:\n"(1) In general\n    An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\n        (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\n            (i) a qualifying child of the individual (as defined in section 152(c)), but not if such child-\n                (I) is married at the close of the taxpayer\'s taxable year, and\n                (II) is not a dependent of such individual by reason of section 152(b)(2)"\n\n### §151(c) Additional exemption for dependents\nLine 65:\n"(c) Additional exemption for dependents\n    An exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year."\n\n### §151(d)(1) Exemption amount\nLines 69-74:\n"(1) In general\n    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \'exemption amount\' means $2,000."\n\n### §63(c)(2)(B) Basic standard deduction\nLines 389-391:\n"(B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or"\n\n## Reasoning\n\n**Step 1: Determine Alice\'s filing status**\n\n- Alice\'s spouse Bob died on July 9, 2014 (case fact)\n- For the 2017 taxable year, the two years immediately preceding are 2015 and 2016\n- Under §2(a)(1)(A), a surviving spouse\'s spouse must have died "during either of the two years immediately preceding the taxable year"\n- Since Bob died in 2014 (not 2015 or 2016), Alice does NOT qualify as a surviving spouse for 2017\n\n**Step 2: Check if Alice qualifies as head of household**\n\n- Alice is not married at the close of her 2017 taxable year (Bob died in 2014)\n- Alice is not a surviving spouse (as established above)\n- Alice furnished over half the cost of maintaining the home where Charlie lived from 2004 to 2019 (case fact: "From 2004 to 2019, Alice furnished the costs of maintaining the home")\n- Charlie is Alice\'s child (born October 9, 2000), so Charlie is a qualifying child under §152(c)\n- Under §2(b)(1), Alice qualifies as head of household\n\n**Step 3: Calculate deductions**\n\n- Standard deduction for head of household: $4,400 (§63(c)(2)(B))\n- Personal exemptions:\n  - Alice\'s own exemption: $2,000 (§151(d)(1))\n  - Charlie\'s exemption as dependent: $2,000 (§151(c))\n  - Total exemptions: $2,000 + $2,000 = $4,000\n\n**Step 4: Calculate taxable income**\n\n- Gross income: $25,561 (case fact)\n- Taxable income = Gross income - Standard deduction - Personal exemptions\n- Taxable income = $25,561 - $4,400 - $4,000 = $17,161\n\n**Step 5: Calculate tax**\n\n- Taxable income of $17,161 is not over $29,600\n- Under §1(b)(i), tax is 15% of taxable income\n- Tax = 15% × $17,161 = $2,574.15\n- Rounding to whole dollar: $2,574\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 2574\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
