iduals filing separate returns.\n\n**Step 2: Exemptions (§151(b) and §151(d)(1))**\n- Exemption amount = $2,000 (line 72)\n- Taxpayer exemption = $2,000\n- Spouse exemption = $2,000 (Bob has no gross income per §151(b))\n- Total exemptions = $2,000 + $2,000 = $4,000\n\n**Step 3: Standard Deduction (§152)**\n- Basic standard deduction for "any other case" (married filing separately) = $3,000 (line 396, §152(c)(4)(C))\n- Additional standard deduction for aged = $600 (Alice is 67, over 65 per §152(f)(1)(A))\n- Total standard deduction = $3,000 + $600 = $3,600\n\n**Step 4: Taxable Income**\nTaxable income = Gross income - Exemptions - Standard deduction\nTaxable income = $36,266 - $4,000 - $3,600 = $28,666\n\n**Step 5: Tax Calculation (§1(d))**\nTaxable income of $28,666 falls in bracket (ii): over $18,450 but not over $44,575\nTax = $2,767.50 + 28% of excess over $18,450\nTax = $2,767.50 + 0.28 × ($28,666 - $18,450)\nTax = $2,767.50 + 0.28 × $10,216\nTax = $2,767.50 + $2,860.48\nTax = $5,627.98\n\nRounded to whole number: $5,628\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 5628\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
