Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt << \'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\nSection 247: "There is hereby imposed on every employer (as defined in section 3306(a)) for each calendar year an excise tax, with respect to having individuals in his employ, equal to 6 percent of the total wages (as defined in section 3306(b)) paid by such employer during the calendar year with respect to employment (as defined in section 3306(c))."\n\nSection 269: "(A) during the calendar year or the preceding calendar year paid wages of $20,000 or more for agricultural labor, or"\n\nSection 72: "Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \'exemption amount\' means $2,000."\n\nSection 395: "(C) $3,000 in any other case."\n\nSection 37: "(v) $79,772, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000."\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. Alice is an unmarried individual (not stated to be married, so uses unmarried tax brackets in Section 1(c)).\n\n2. Alice paid agricultural labor wages totaling $31,350:\n   - Bob: 10 occasions × $550 = $5,500\n   - Cameron: 11 occasions × $550 = $6,050\n   - Dan: 9 occasions × $550 = $4,950\n   - Emily: 10 occasions × $550 = $5,500\n   - Fred: 9 occasions × $550 = $4,950\n   - George: 8 occasions × $550 = $4,400\n   - Total: $31,350 (computed with python3)\n\n3. Under Section 269, Alice is an employer because she paid wages of $20,000 or more ($31,350 > $20,000).\n\n4. Under Section 247, Alice owes an excise tax of 6% of total wages: 0.06 × $31,350 = $1,881.\n\n5. Taxable income calculation:\n   - Gross income: $567,192 (given fact)\n   - Less standard deduction: $3,000 (Section 395(C) for unmarried)\n   - Less personal exemption: $2,000 (Section 72)\n   - Taxable income: $567,192 - $3,000 - $2,000 = $562,192\n\n6. Income tax (Section 37, unmarried over $250,000):\n   - Base tax: $79,772\n   - Excess over $250,000: $562,192 - $250,000 = $312,192\n   - Additional tax: 0.396 × $312,192 = $123,628.032\n   - Total income tax: $79,772 + $123,628.032 = $203,400.032\n\n7. Total tax = Income tax + Employer excise tax\n   - Total tax = $203,400.032 + $1,881 = $205,281.032\n   - Rounded to whole number: $205,281\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 205281\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
