Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt << \'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\n§1(a)(iii) (lines 15): "(iii) $20,165, plus 31% of the excess over $89,150 if the taxable income is over $89,150 but not over $140,000;"\n\n§152(b)(2)(C) and §152(g)(7) (line 430): "(ii) by substituting "$12,000" for "$3,000" in subparagraph (C)."\n\n§152(f)(1) (line 444): "The taxpayer shall be entitled to an additional amount of $600-"\n\n§151(d)(3) (line 90): "In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026, the term "exemption amount" means zero."\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. **Filing status**: Alice and Bob are married (married since Feb 3, 2017) and file jointly in 2019. They are subject to §1(a) tax rates for married individuals filing joint returns.\n\n2. **Standard deduction**: Under §152(b)(2)(C) and §152(g)(7), the standard deduction for married filing jointly in 2019 (taxable year beginning after Dec 31, 2017) is $12,000.\n\n3. **Additional standard deduction for age**: Alice was born March 2, 1950, so she is 69 years old in 2019 (over 65). Under §152(f)(1), she is entitled to an additional standard deduction of $600. Bob was born March 3, 1955, so he is 64 years old (not over 65).\n\n   Total standard deduction = $12,000 + $600 = $12,600\n\n4. **Personal exemptions**: Under §151(d)(3), for taxable years beginning after December 31, 2017 and before January 1, 2026, the exemption amount is zero. Therefore, no personal exemptions are allowed in 2019.\n\n5. **Taxable income calculation**:\n   - Gross income = $113,580 (Bob\'s income) + $0 (Alice\'s income) = $113,580\n   - Taxable income = $113,580 - $12,600 - $0 = $100,980\n\n6. **Tax calculation**: Taxable income of $100,980 falls in the bracket "over $89,150 but not over $140,000" under §1(a)(iii).\n   - Tax = $20,165 + 31% × ($100,980 - $89,150)\n   - Tax = $20,165 + 0.31 × $11,830\n   - Tax = $20,165 + $3,667.30\n   - Tax = $23,832.30\n\n   Rounded to whole dollar: $23,832\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 23832\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
