 this paragraph if such individual is-\n\n        (A) a child of the taxpayer or a descendant of such a child, or\n\n        (B) a brother, sister, stepbrother, or stepsister of the taxpayer or a descendant of any such relative.\n\n    (3) Age requirements\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(C), an individual meets the requirements of this paragraph if such individual is younger than the taxpayer claiming such individual as a qualifying child and is less than 25 years old at the end of the taxable year.\n[Lines 114-158]\n\n§63. Taxable income defined\n\n(c) Standard deduction\n\n    (2) Basic standard deduction\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\n\n        (A) 200 percent of the dollar amount in effect under subparagraph (C) for the taxable year in the case of-\n\n            (i) a joint return, or\n\n            (ii) a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\n\n        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\n\n        (C) $3,000 in any other case.\n[Lines 379-396]\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. Alice and Bob filed jointly in 2013. Alice was alive during 2013 (died July 9, 2014), so they are subject to "Married individuals filing joint returns" under §1(a) (lines 1-17).\n\n2. Gross income calculation:\n   - Alice\'s income: $65,400 (case fact)\n   - Bob\'s income: $56,400 (case fact)\n   - Total gross income: $65,400 + $56,400 = $121,800\n\n3. Standard deduction for joint return:\n   - Under §63(c)(2)(A), the basic standard deduction for a joint return is 200% of $3,000 (the amount in §63(c)(2)(C))\n   - Standard deduction = 2 × $3,000 = $6,000\n\n4. Personal exemptions:\n   - Under §151(d)(1), the exemption amount is $2,000 per person (line 67)\n   - Alice: $2,000 (taxpayer)\n   - Bob: $2,000 (spouse)\n   - Charlie: $2,000 (dependent child under §152)\n   - Total exemptions = $2,000 × 3 = $6,000\n\n5. Charlie\'s qualifying child status under §152(c) (lines 114-158):\n   - (c)(2)(A): Charlie is Bob\'s child - YES (Charlie born October 9, 2000)\n   - (c)(1)(B): Charlie has same principal place of abode as Bob for more than half the year - YES (Bob and Charlie lived together 2004-2019 per case facts)\n   - (c)(1)(C): Charlie is younger than Bob and less than 25 years old at end of 2013 - YES (Charlie was 12-13 years old in 2013)\n   - (c)(1)(E): Charlie did not file a joint return - YES (Charlie is a child)\n   - Charlie qualifies as a dependent\n\n6. Taxable income:\n   - Taxable income = Gross income - Standard deduction - Exemptions\n   - Taxable income = $121,800 - $6,000 - $6,000 = $109,800\n\n7. Tax calculation:\n   - Taxable income of $109,800 falls in the bracket "over $89,150 but not over $140,000" under §1(a)(iii) (line 13)\n   - Tax = $20,165 + 31% of ($109,800 - $89,150)\n   - Tax = $20,165 + 0.31 × $20,650\n   - Tax = $20,165 + $6,401.50\n   - Tax = $26,566.50\n\n8. Rounding to whole number: $26,567\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 26567\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
