rviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-"\n"        (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-"\n"            (ii) any other person who is a dependent of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such person under section 151, or"\n"        (B) maintains a household which constitutes for such taxable year the principal place of abode of the father or mother of the taxpayer, if the taxpayer is entitled to a deduction for the taxable year for such father or mother under section 151."\n\n§1. Tax imposed (line 1)\n\n(b) Heads of households (lines 44-54):\n"    (iii) $17,544, plus 31% of the excess over $76,400 if the taxable income is over $76,400 but not over $127,500;"\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. **Charlie qualifies as a qualifying relative (dependent):**\n   - Charlie is Alice\'s father → relationship test met under §152(d)(2)(C) (line 165)\n   - Charlie has no income in 2015 → meets §152(d)(1)(B) (line 153)\n   - Charlie is not a qualifying child (born 1994, age 21 in 2015, does not meet age requirements of §152(c)(3)) → meets §152(d)(1)(D) (line 155)\n\n2. **Bob qualifies as a qualifying relative (dependent):**\n   - Bob is Charlie\'s brother, making him Alice\'s uncle → relationship test met under §152(d)(2)(F) (line 168)\n   - Bob has no income in 2015 → meets §152(d)(1)(B) (line 153)\n   - Bob is not a qualifying child (born 1992, age 23 in 2015, does not meet age requirements of §152(c)(3)) → meets §152(d)(1)(D) (line 155)\n\n3. **Alice qualifies as head of household:**\n   - Alice is not married at the close of 2015\n   - Alice maintains a household for her father Charlie, whom she is entitled to deduct under section 151 → §2(b)(1)(B) (lines 201-238)\n\n4. **Exemption calculation:**\n   - Exemption amount = $2,000 per §151(d)(1) (line 72)\n   - Number of exemptions = 3 (Alice + Charlie + B