Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<\'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\nSection 7703(a)(1) - Determination of marital status (line 509):\n"(1) the determination of whether an individual is married shall be made as of the close of his taxable year"\n\nSection 1(c)(v) - Tax brackets for unmarried individuals (line 37):\n"(v) $79,772, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000."\n\nSection 63(c)(2)(C) - Basic standard deduction for unmarried individuals (line 396):\n"(C) $3,000 in any other case."\n\nSection 151(d)(1) - Exemption amount (line 72):\n"Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term "exemption amount" means $2,000."\n\nSection 151(d)(3)(B) - Exemption phaseout (line 86):\n"For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term "applicable percentage" means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer\'s adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent."\n\nSection 68(b)(1)(C) - Applicable amount for unmarried individuals (line 491):\n"(C) $250,000 in the case of an individual who is not married and who is not a surviving spouse or head of household"\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. Marital Status: Alice and Bob were married from Feb 3rd, 1997 to Oct 30th, 2001. Per Section 7703(a)(1), marital status is determined as of the close of the taxable year (2014). Since Alice was divorced in 2001, she is unmarried in 2014.\n\n2. Standard Deduction: Per Section 63(c)(2)(C), Alice (unmarried, "any other case") gets a basic standard deduction of $3,000.\n\n3. Personal Exemption Phaseout:\n   - AGI (gross income): $718,791 (case fact)\n   - Applicable amount for unmarried: $250,000 (Section 68(b)(1)(C), line 491)\n   - Excess: $718,791 - $250,000 = $468,791\n   - Number of $2,500 fractions: ceil($468,791 / $2,500) = 188\n   - Phaseout percentage: 188 × 2% = 376%, capped at 100% (Section 151(d)(3)(B), line 86)\n   - Exemption amount: $2,000 × (1 - 100%) = $0\n\n4. Taxable Income: $718,791 - $3,000 - $0 = $715,791\n\n5. Tax Calculation (Section 1(c)(v), line 37):\n   - Taxable income $715,791 exceeds $250,000\n   - Tax = $79,772 + 39.6% × ($715,791 - $250,000)\n   - Tax = $79,772 + 0.396 × $465,791\n   - Tax = $79,772 + $184,453.236 = $264,225.236\n   - Rounded to whole number: $264,225\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 264225\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
