Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<\'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\n§1. Tax imposed - subsection (b) Heads of households (lines 25-44):\n\n"(b) Heads of households\n\nThere is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every head of a household (as defined in section 2(b)) a tax determined in accordance with the following:\n\n    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $29,600;\n    (ii) $4,440, plus 28% of the excess over $29,600 if the taxable income is over $29,600 but not over $76,400;"\n\n§2. Definitions and special rules - subsection (b) Definition of head of household (lines 182-230):\n\n"(b) Definition of head of household\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    An individual shall be considered a head of a household if, and only if, such individual is not married at the close of his taxable year, is not a surviving spouse (as defined in subsection (a)), and either-\n\n        (A) maintains as his home a household which constitutes for more than one-half of such taxable year the principal place of abode, as a member of such household, of-\n\n            (i) a qualifying child of the individual (as defined in section 152(c)), but not if such child-\n\n                (I) is married at the close of the taxpayer\'s taxable year, and\n\n                (II) is not a dependent of such individual by reason of section 152(b)(2) or"\n\n§152. Dependent defined - subsection (c) Qualifying child (lines 95-133):\n\n"(c) Qualifying child\n\nFor purposes of this section-\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    The term "qualifying child" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual-\n\n        (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\n\n        (B) who has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year,\n\n        (C) who meets the age requirements of paragraph (3), and\n\n        (E) who has not filed a joint return (other than only for a claim of refund) with the individual\'s spouse for the taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins.\n\n    (2) Relationship\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(A), an individual bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in this paragraph if such individual is-\n\n        (A) a child of the taxpayer or a descendant of such a child, or"\n\n§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions - subsection (d) Exemption amount (lines 117-128):\n\n"(d) Exemption amount\n\nFor purposes of this section-\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term "exemption amount" means $2,000."\n\n§162. Standard deduction - subsection (c)(2) Basic standard deduction (lines 378-396):\n\n"(2) Basic standard deduction\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\n\n        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or"\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. **Filing Status**: Bob is unmarried (no spouse mentioned in the facts). Bob maintains a household that constitutes the principal place of abode of his son Charlie for more than one-half of 2015. Charlie is Bob\'s qualifying child under §152(c) because Charlie is Bob\'s child (§152(c)(2)(A)), has the same principal place of abode (§152(c)(1)(B)), and Charlie is age 1 in 2015 (born Jun 29, 2014), which is less than 25 years old at the end of the taxable year (§152(c)(3)). Charlie has not filed a joint return (§152(c)(1)(E)). Therefore, Bob qualifies as Head of Household under §2(b)(1)(A)(i).\n\n2. **Personal Exemptions**: Bob is entitled to a personal exemption of $2,000 for himself under §151(b). Bob is also entitled to a personal exemption of $2,000 for Charlie as a dependent under §151(c). Total personal exemptions = $2,000 + $2,000 = $4,000.\n\n3. **Standard Deduction**: As a Head of Household who takes the standard deduction, Bob is entitled to a basic standard deduction of $4,400 under §162(c)(2)(B). Bob is age 27 in 2015 (born Feb 7, 1988), so he is not entitled to any additional standard deduction for being aged or blind.\n\n4. **Taxable Income Calculation**:\n   - Gross income: $43,591 (given fact)\n   - Less: Standard deduction: $4,400 (§162(c)(2)(B))\n   - Less: Personal exemptions: $4,000 (§151)\n   - Taxable income = $43,591 - $4,400 - $4,000 = $35,191\n\n5. **Tax Calculation**: Under §1(b)(ii), for Head of Household with taxable income over $29,600 but not over $76,400, the tax is $4,440 plus 28% of the excess over $29,600.\n   - Excess over $29,600 = $35,191 - $29,600 = $5,591\n   - Tax = $4,440 + 0.28 × $5,591 = $4,440 + $1,565.48 = $6,005.48\n   - Rounded to whole number: $6,005\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 6005\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
