idual\'s spouse for the taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins.\n\n    (2) Relationship\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(A), an individual bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in this paragraph if such individual is-\n\n        (A) a child of the taxpayer or a descendant of such a child, or"\n\n§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions - subsection (d) Exemption amount (lines 66-71):\n\n"(d) Exemption amount\n\nFor purposes of this section-\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term "exemption amount" means $2,000."\n\n§162. Standard deduction - subsection (c)(2) Basic standard deduction (lines 372-396):\n\n"(2) Basic standard deduction\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\n\n        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or"\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. **Filing Status**: Bob is unmarried (no spouse mentioned in the facts). Bob maintains a household that constitutes the principal place of abode of his son Charlie for more than one-half of 2015. Charlie is Bob\'s qualifying child under §152(c) because Charlie is Bob\'s child (§152(c)(2)(A)), has the same principal place of abode (§152(c)(1)(B)), and Charlie is age 1 in 2015 (born Jun 29, 2014), which is less than 25 years old at the end of the taxable year (§152(c)(3)). Charlie has not filed a joint return (§152(c)(1)(E)). Therefore, Bob qualifies as Head of Household under §2(b)(1)(A)(i).\n\n2. **Personal Exemptions**: Bob is entitled to a personal exemption of $2,000 for himself under §151(b). Bob is also entitled to a personal exemption of $2,000 for Charlie as a dependent under §151(c). The facts do not state that Alice claims Charlie, so Charlie\'s exemption amount is not zero under §151(d)(2). Total personal exemptions = $2,000 + $2,000 = $4,000.\n\n3. **Standard Deduction**: As a Head of Household who takes the standard deduction, Bob is entitled to a basic standard deduction of $4,400 under §162(c)(2)(B). Bob is age 27 in 2015 (born Feb 7, 1988), so he is not entitled to any additional standard deduction for being aged or blind.\n\n4. **Taxable Income Calculation**:\n   - Gross income: $43,591 (given fact)\n   - Less: Standard deduction: $4,400 (§162(c)(2)(B))\n   - Less: Personal exemptions: $4,000 (§151)\n   - Taxable income = $43,591 - $4,400 - $4,000 = $35,191\n\n5. **Tax Calculation**: Under §1(b)(ii), for Head of Household with taxable income over $29,600 but not over $76,400, the tax is $4,440 plus 28% of the excess over $29,600.\n   - Excess over $29,600 = $35,191 - $29,600 = $5,591\n   - Tax = $4,440 + 0.28 × $5,591 = $4,440 + $1,565.48 = $6,005.48\n   - Rounded to whole number: $6,005\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 6005\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
